{
  "A0100": "From steps 15–46, A0100 held a broadly northbound intercept while repeatedly commanding descent and speed increase, converting altitude from about 6.0 km toward 5.7 km as the opposing southbound formation closed. Its small early heading corrections appear aimed at keeping an attack lane rather than breaking contact. At step 47 its ammunition falls from two to one and A01002 appears; this coincides with B0200’s missile expenditure, indicating a likely reciprocal long-range exchange, although targets are unrecorded. A0100 then sustained right-30 commands through step 70, turning progressively from north toward east-northeast while its missile continued northward. This most plausibly reduced its direct exposure after firing while preserving lateral separation and speed. From steps 71–75 it held the altitude command but continued the rightward turn, ending on a markedly eastward escape/repositioning vector rather than pressing straight into the opposing formation.",
  "A0200": "A0200 spent the opening phase, steps 15–46, descending, accelerating, and holding an almost due-north track despite alternating small heading commands. Together with A0100, this maintained closure against the two southbound B aircraft while retaining a compact altitude band and building speed. When A0100 launched and began its major rightward displacement at step 47, A0200 largely continued north, suggesting that it retained the more direct pressure role instead of following the break. Its ammunition decreases from two to one at step 50 and A02002 appears, supporting a missile shot after it had maintained this forward geometry. A0200 did not make a comparably large defensive turn after B01002 appeared at step 52; it continued descending and accelerating to over 300 m/s by step 75. The sequence is most consistent with maintaining attack pressure or missile-support geometry while A0100 created lateral spacing, rather than disengaging with its teammate.",
  "B0100": "B0100 began north of Team A and flew steadily south throughout steps 15–75, descending from roughly 6.14 km to 5.54 km while accelerating from about 232 to 290 m/s. Its track remained close to due south despite the closing geometry, so its principal apparent objective was to preserve a direct intercept lane on the approaching A formation rather than maneuver defensively. The sustained descent and acceleration mirrored Team A’s energy-building dive, reducing altitude while increasing closure and likely helping retain an engagement opportunity. B0100 retained two missiles through step 51, then its count drops to one and B01002 first appears at step 52, after the earlier A0100/B0200 missile exchange and A0200’s subsequent shot. It nevertheless continued straight south after firing, which is most consistent with sustaining forward pressure or missile geometry. No telemetry shows a post-launch break, confirmed target, or missile result before the window ends.",
  "B0200": "B0200 also maintained a southbound, descending approach across the full window, accelerating from about 238 m/s to 291 m/s while giving up altitude from 6.14 km to 5.54 km. This persistent course kept it closing the northern-southern separation with Team A rather than seeking early lateral disengagement. At step 47 its ammunition decreases from two to one and B02002 appears at the same time that A0100 expends a missile. The near-simultaneous launches, followed by A0100’s sustained rightward break, strongly suggest an exchange in the same general engagement sector, though the recorded data do not identify either missile’s target. B0200 itself remained on the southbound attack axis after launch, apparently choosing to retain forward pressure rather than immediately evade. When B0100 fired at step 52, B0200 still continued its direct descent and acceleration, consistent with the B pair sustaining the engagement while their missiles remained active."
}
